      "content": "While high levels of vitamin K are indeed involved in promoting blood clotting, making an unsupervised adjustment to your warfarin dose can be dangerous and unpredictable. Your high INR signifies that your blood is clotting more than it should, which can prevent clot formation in case you need one, increasing the risk of bleeding. A temporary solution like taking a K supplement or eating a high-K diet isn’t appropriate because it could dangerously overshoot your clotting ability, risking bleeding issues unexpectedly. The safest course of action is to contact your healthcare provider as soon as you can discuss your INR reading. In the meantime, continue taking your warfarin as prescribed, and avoid eating large quantities of vitamin K or taking vitamin K supplements. If your situation worsens before Monday, seek immediate medical assistance.",
